course: dictionary
lesson: 14130
title: A word for rock scientists
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mineralogist is a scientist who studies minerals. A mineral is a natural solid, such as quartz, salt or gold, and minerals are the materials that make up rocks.
explain: Context gives you clues. «The mineralogist scratched the stone with a steel nail to test how hard it was.» Scratching and testing tell you the job is about checking what a stone is made of and how it behaves.
explain: Mineralogists look at a mineral's hardness, colour, streak and crystal shape. Mineralogy is the name of the science itself, and a geologist is a related scientist who studies rocks and the Earth as a whole.
fact: A mineralogist is a scientist who studies minerals.
fact: A mineral is a natural solid material, such as quartz, salt or gold.
fact: Mineralogists test hardness, colour, streak and crystal shape.
fact: Mineralogy is the science of minerals.
fact: A geologist studies rocks and the Earth as a whole.
exercise: What is a mineralogist? | A person who sells gold jewellery | *A scientist who studies minerals | A cook who makes crystal sweets | A doctor who treats broken bones
exercise: «The mineralogist scratched the stone with a steel nail to test how hard it was.» What is the mineralogist testing? | *How hard the stone is | How old the nail is | Whether the stone can float | How heavy the stone is in a bag
exercise: Maya says, «I want to be a mineralogist, because I love crystals.» What might Maya like to study? | Music and songs | Old cooking recipes | Weather forecasts | *Minerals and their crystal shapes
test: Which word means the science of minerals? | Biology | Geology | *Mineralogy | Astronomy
test: Which of these is a mineral? | *Quartz | Feather | Cheese | Wood
exam: Which scientist studies rocks and the whole Earth, not just minerals? | A dentist | A pilot | *A geologist | A mineralogist
